    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #50 Quantitative Adjustment: EOD Decay & Fee Drag Mitigation\nForensic analysis of Cycle #49 revealed that the strategy was gross-profitable (+\u20b926.98) in OOS testing but pushed into net deficit (-\u20b912.63) due to \u20b939.61 in statutory fees and EOD square-off decay. Specifically, 50% of losing trades were midday/afternoon entries in lower-beta names (ITC, TATASTEEL, ICICIBANK) that lacked the intraday range to reach the 1.45% target before the 15:15 IST cutoff. To convert stalled afternoon drift into realized wins and insulate the \u20b910,000 capital base from fee erosion, `min_target_pct` is compressed to **1.15%** and `breakeven_trigger_r` is pulled forward to **0.95R**. Simultaneously, `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` is elevated to **2.90x** to reject low-conviction midday liquidity sweeps, while `min_sl_pct` is calibrated to **0.55%** to maintain an optimal >2:1 reward-to-risk ratio."
